<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<IncludeEstTaxInQuoteCPQSettings xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- "Add Estimated Taxes to Quotes and Orders" is off by default. With it on, a Sales
         Price Amendment that lowers the price fails with "TaxAmount can't have a negative
         value" (label AmountNegative; {0} can also be TotalAmount, TotalAmountWithTax or
         ExemptAmount). Estimated tax always goes to the engine as a Debit, and the amended
         line's total is a credit. Core's engine-response validator rejects a negative tax,
         total or total-with-tax amount on a Debit response. Returning 0 tax from the mock
         adapter did not clear it, because its totals were still negative. Tax is skipped
         only when a line has a negative quantity, and then for the whole transaction.
         Verified on a 264.7 org, 2026-10-14. This setting covers quotes and orders; invoice
         tax goes through Billing's tax path.
         Deployed by deploy_quote_est_tax_settings (prepare_core step 18), which writes true
         instead when quote_est_tax is on. It's kept out of unpackaged/pre so a re-run of
         deploy_pre, or ensure_pricing_schedules' redeploy of pre/2_settings, can't turn it
         back off on an org built with the flag. -->
    <enableQuoteEstimatedTaxCPQ>false</enableQuoteEstimatedTaxCPQ>
</IncludeEstTaxInQuoteCPQSettings>
